WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.901
-Our next guest is a very funny
comedian who will be headlining

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.200
Carnegie Hall with his show

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.534
"Gary Gulman: Born on
Third Base" this Saturday,

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:10.501
November 13th, as part of
the New York Comedy Festival.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:13.000
Please welcome back to the show
our friend Gary Gulman.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.701
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:25.634
♪♪

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.667
Welcome back. How are you?

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.334
-It's nice to be back.
I'm terrific.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.634
-Carnegie Hall.
That's a big deal.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:33.067
-I was hoping
you would bring that up.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:33.934
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.367
-Yeah, thank you.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:38.501
Because I don't want it
to just be my manager

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:40.067
and his mother in the audience.

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.901
So you're all invited
to Carnegie Hall.

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
-But it must be --

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.267
I mean, you know, all comedians
have, through the course of

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.501
their career, played
some really low-rent rooms.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.033
It must feel like a real --

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:53.501
This is the right arc to end up
in an iconic room like that.

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:56.400
-It's the first venue
my mother has heard of.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.901
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.901 --> 00:01:01.033
-She's not familiar with
Gutbusters in Tampa,

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:03.667
and the Yuk Yuk's chain.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.400
So this is very exciting.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.601
She can tell all her friends
that I'm performing in a place

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:10.133
they've been familiar with.
-That's fantastic.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:11.934
And you're living in
New York now.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.601
-Yes.
-You're up in Harlem.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.067
How is it?
-It's fantastic.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.234
The nicest people.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:18.634
They tell me to have
a blessed day, every day.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:22.801
I live at 139,000th and...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:24.534
And Malcolm X.

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:26.901
And people assume --

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:30.033
Well, my wife is a black woman,
so I'm her plus-one.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.234
So they assume that
my neighborhood is gentrified.

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:36.100
But I think they're thinking
further down towards the park.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.267
There's a Whole Foods at
120th and Malcolm Gladwell.

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:40.701
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:42.367
That's a little bit
more gentrified.

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:46.701
-Yes, and then at 110th, it's
actually Malcolm in the Middle.

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:48.734
-Oh, I understand.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:51.901
-Those are the famous Malcolms.

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.000
-The famous white --
whiter Malcolms.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.300
-I left out
Forbes and McDowell there.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.033
So I apologize to their fans
and estates.

00:01:58.033 --> 00:01:59.834
-I want to ask about
the name of your special,

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.634
'cause, you know, you did
"The Great Depresh,"

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.801
which is absolutely wonderful
and I can't recommend it enough,

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.901
where you talked about issues
like anxiety and depression.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:10.667
What is behind the name
"Born on Third Base"?

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:15.000
-Well, I am very blessed
in that, one,

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.467
I suffer from depression during
a time when they could treat it.

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.133
And a hundred years ago,

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:22.167
they would just throw me away
and lock the door.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.200
And so I'm very grateful
for that.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.334
Also, I grew up in the '70s
a white male in New England.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:29.968
So I had advantages.

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:32.400
I'm 6'6", and I ran really fast,

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.801
so I was able to get
a scholarship to college.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:36.601
So I was born on third base.

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:40.167
As poor as we were growing up --
and we were poor --

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:42.901
the great thing was we didn't
feel poor because my father --

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:46.934
a mensch -- and I just want to
keep with the Jewish theme

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:48.567
that we have going here.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:50.334
-It's a very thematic episode,
yeah.

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:53.000
-This is -- You thought
Hanukkah was early?

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.334
No.
It starts before Thanksgiving.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:56.934
[ Laughter ]
This is incredible.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:58.934
-This is a pre-Hanukkah party,
yeah.

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:00.300
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.801
My father had this policy
that made us feel less poor.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:05.133
He would say, "If there's
something you really want,

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:07.467
just ask for it.
We'll try to find the money."

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:09.934
And then, of course,
like any dad, he would talk us

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:13.133
out of wanting whatever it was
that we wanted.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:15.434
Like, one year, I wanted to
play hockey,

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:16.667
which, as a New Englander,
you know, it's huge.

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:17.934
-Of course. Yep.

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:20.000
-And so he said, "If you
really want to play hockey,

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.501
we'll try to find the money
for you to play this sport

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.400
you've shown no potential in."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.868
"Not only have you shown
no potential,

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:32.067
Jews have acquitted themselves
quite poorly in this sport."

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:34.834
And then he pulled out
this sports almanac

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:36.000
with the Hockey Hall of Fame.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.868
He said, "Let's count
the Jewish players."

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:39.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:42.968
"Ready? Done.
There are zero Jewish players."

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:44.634
He said, "Just for
a point of comparison,

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:47.400
more Jews have been
the Messiah."

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:53.567
"Do you understand that
you're more likely to be Jesus?

00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:55.901
You are more likely
to walk on water

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.534
than you are to skate on it."

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:03.000
-How have you -- You know,
I think a lot of people were

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.634
interested in how behavior
would change

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.033
over the course of this
pandemic, and as we're coming

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:09.133
back to normal, do you --
were your predictions

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:10.400
correct in how people...?
-No.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.567
I really thought people
were going to be nicer.

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:14.801
-Yeah.
-And then I went to Chipotle

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:16.167
soon after.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:17.968
I go there every other day
anyhow.

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:19.267
It's delicious.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:21.601
And the people who work there
are so composed

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:24.133
despite the fact that they
deal with this all day long.

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:27.367
Ready? "Corn, corn, black beans,
brown rice."

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.667
Just people wagging their finger
at them

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:32.200
to assemble their burrito.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.767
Or their bowl.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:37.133
You got to be so careful, Seth.

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:40.667
-In this day and age,
you got to be so careful.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:44.133
-You say burrito, leaving out
the bowl people, the next day,

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:45.334
the people are on -- yes, yes.

00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:47.868
-They're like,
"Hey, bowl erasure."

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:49.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:51.167
-Right now somebody is angry
because I'm not doing

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.567
the manual typewriter correctly.

00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:56.601
-Right, there's -- yeah.
-They'll be writing letters.

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.501
And so they come in there,
and I just want to tell you,

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:02.868
if you go to Chipotle,
you don't have to point.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:05.267
They know where the corn is.

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:06.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:08.767
You found it.
You don't even work here.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:11.400
How would they not know
where the corn is?

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.334
Just give them the benefit of
the doubt.

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:18.033
Say "corn," and then,
if they look baffled...

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:21.200
[ Laughter ]
...then add the visual aid.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.801
But until -- I'm too sen--

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:26.000
I wouldn't last a shift
at Chipotle.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.267
Somebody would come in, "Corn."

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:30.100
"Oh, is that --
Is that where the corn --

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.567
Brenda, I found the corn!"

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:35.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:36.801
"It was with
the other toppings.

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:39.234
It's always the last place
you look."

00:05:39.234 --> 00:05:40.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:41.968
-It's so lovely to see you
again, Gary.

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:43.100
-Same here, Seth.
-Thanks for being here.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:45.000
Congratulations. Carnegie Hall!

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:49.133
-For more info on tour dates,
go to garygulman.com.

